MAN(1)                     Funny CLI Manual                     MAN(1)

NAME
    man — Display manuals for commands, or for man itself if you're feeling recursive.

SYNOPSIS
    man [command]

DESCRIPTION
    The 'man' command is your friendly neighborhood guide to all things CLI.
    It tells you what other commands do, how to use them, and occasionally how to
    make yourself a sandwich (not guaranteed).

USAGE
    > man            # Shows a list of all commands, in case you forgot or are feeling lost.
    > man <command>  # Shows a detailed explanation of the command.
    > man man        # The universe folds in on itself, and you see this manual. Brace yourself.

FUN FACTS
    - Using 'man man' is technically called "metadocumentation."
    - It may cause mild existential crises in inexperienced programmers.
    - Repeated use can lead to spontaneous laughter and increased CLI wisdom.

EXAMPLES
    > man ls
        Lists files in a directory. Also great for showing off your dotfiles.
    > man cd
        Changes your directory. Like teleportation, but slower.
    > man man
        Congratulations! You just stared into the abyss. The abyss blinked. You blinked back.

SEE ALSO
    help(1), ls(1), cd(1)
    Remember, 'man man' is the apex of CLI humor. Respect it.

